// Keymap document owned by the `command_palette` example.
//
// It replaces Fairy Dust's shipped document, so it binds `palette::open` as well as the
// two `example::` commands the example declares with `command!`.
//
// `example::home` takes `secondary-shift-h` rather than `secondary-h`, because on macOS
// `secondary` is Cmd and Cmd+H is the system chord that hides the application — the
// example would never see it.
//
// The second block deliberately misspells `context` as `contxt`. That is an authoring
// mistake the keymap reports as an advisory rather than a failure, so the example opens
// with one advisory row above its query field and still runs every binding — which is
// what the palette's failure rows are there to show.
{
  "bindings": [
    {
      "bindings": {
        "secondary-p": "palette::open",
        "secondary-shift-h": "example::home",
        "secondary-k": "example::swap_camera"
      }
    },
    {
      "contxt": "global",
      "bindings": {
        "secondary-shift-k": "example::swap_camera"
      }
    }
  ]
}
